{"causes": ["The death of Hetman Bohdan Khmelnytsky in 1657 plunged the Cossack Hetmanate into a period of severe internal strife known as the Ruin.", "The Treaty of Pereyaslav in 1654 established a complex and often contested relationship between the Cossack Hetmanate and the Tsardom of Russia, creating a powerful external influence on Ukrainian politics.", "Hetman Ivan Vyhovsky's pro-Polish policies and the Treaty of Hadiach (1658) provoked strong opposition among many Cossack regiments, leading to a major civil war."], "effects": ["Ivan Bezpaly's brief hetmanship significantly solidified the Tsardom of Russia's influence and control over Left-Bank Ukraine.", "His leadership contributed to the political and territorial fragmentation of the Cossack Hetmanate into pro-Polish and pro-Russian factions.", "Bezpaly's actions helped establish a precedent for Muscovite-backed hetmans, ultimately leading to the gradual erosion of Cossack autonomy and the absorption of Left-Bank Ukraine into the Russian Empire."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "ivan-bezpaly", "sourceName": "Ivan Bezpaly", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "the-ruin-ukraine", "targetName": "The Ruin (Ukraine)", "context": "Ivan Bezpaly was a key figure and faction leader during the turbulent period of civil war and foreign intervention known as the Ruin in Ukraine."}, {"sourceSlug": "tsardom-of-russia", "sourceName": "Tsardom of Russia", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "ivan-bezpaly", "targetName": "Ivan Bezpaly", "context": "The Tsardom of Russia heavily influenced Ivan Bezpaly's political career and supported his election as acting Hetman of the Left-Bank."}, {"sourceSlug": "ivan-bezpaly", "sourceName": "Ivan Bezpaly", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "tsardom-of-russia", "targetName": "Tsardom of Russia", "context": "Ivan Bezpaly actively collaborated with the Tsardom of Russia, leading the pro-Russian faction in Eastern Ukraine and pledging allegiance to the Tsar."}, {"sourceSlug"